From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lemelson <97357844+Lemelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:07:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] es_out: do not count a user pause as PCR lateness

While the input is paused, the input clock is anchored at the pause
date (i_pause_date) and shifted by the pause length on resume. PCR
updates received while paused, for example during the buffering of a
paused seek, are nevertheless converted with vlc_tick_now(). The longer
the pause, the later the PCR looks: input_clock_Update() reports it as
late, es_out resets buffering, and playback skips past the requested
target.

The rebuffering work (ec61ad7474, be5cd7a749) already uses the frozen
pause date for download stalls (b_rebuffering). Use it for every paused
state, through the existing EsOutIsPaused() helper (user pause or
rebuffering). The pause anchor, locking and rate handling are
unchanged.

Reproduction (libvlccore at 4ca4eb0c3e with the decoder first-picture
patch, macOS arm64): play, pause for about 2 s, then seek while paused.
LLDB shows a late PCR of 1,005,561 us for a 2 s pause, then a buffering
reset; the displayed picture is past the requested target.

Narrow change, second upstream candidate together with the decoder
first-picture fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/es_out.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
index 1617513..87041ae 100644
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -3723,9 +3723,9 @@ static int EsOutVaControlLocked(es_out_sys_t *p_sys, input_source_t *source,
         const bool b_low_delay = priv->b_low_delay;
         bool b_extra_buffering_allowed = !b_low_delay && EsOutIsExtraBufferingAllowed(p_sys);
         bool buffering = EsOutIsBuffering(p_sys) || p_sys->p_next_frame_es != NULL;
-        /* Do not account the download stall as clock lateness. The input
-         * clock will shift this frozen system date when rebuffering ends. */
-        const vlc_tick_t system_now = p_sys->b_rebuffering
+        /* Do not account a user pause or download stall as clock lateness.
+         * Both use the frozen pause origin until the input clock resumes. */
+        const vlc_tick_t system_now = EsOutIsPaused(p_sys)
                                     ? p_sys->i_pause_date : vlc_tick_now();
         vlc_tick_t i_late = input_clock_Update(
                             p_pgrm->p_input_clock,
